    "evidence": "Re-verified 2026-08-10. The canonical GhoToken is a direct non-proxy deployment (EIP-1967 implementation slot zero), and its verified source exposes ordinary ERC-20 transfer/transferFrom paths without a holder blacklist, balance freeze, seizure, arbitrary-holder burn, or global transfer pause. Aave and Chainlink identify the reviewed non-Ethereum representations as CCIP burn/mint tokens; those bridge controls do not establish a current holder-level restriction on canonical GHO. Aave DAO facilitator and bucket roles affect issuance, not existing-holder transfers. GHO nevertheless resolves as upstream under the >50% reserve-exposure rule: the reviewed reserve composition includes 44.3% mainnet GSM aggregate exposure whose underlying stablecoin identities are not published at slice level, plus 7.4% tracked stataUSDT GSM exposure, so more than 50% of current composition is exposed to stablecoin/GSM freeze surfaces.",
    "reviewer": "OpenAI Codex FreezeWatch consistency review",
    "reviewedAt": "2026-08-10"
